hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16836","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, he said: Abu Ma'shar al-Bara narrated to us, he said: Ibn Harmala narrated to us from Yahya ibn Hind ibn Haritha from his father, and he was among the companions of al-Hudaybiya, and his brother whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ordering his people to fast the day of Ashura, and he is Asma ibn Haritha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him and said: Order your people to fast this day. He said: What if I find them having already eaten? He said: Then let them complete the rest of their day."
